  "caption": "Quinn reached for the top shelf and felt a sharp jab beside the breastbone. Twisting hurt, deep breaths hurt, even hugs felt risky.\n\nFirst stop was the GP, because chest pain always needs the heart checked first. With that cleared, Kay found irritated cartilage where the ribs meet the breastbone. Note: pain on pressing doesn't rule out the heart.\n\nWhat can help: easing off pressing and big twists while staying active, gentle mid-back mobility, warmth and relaxed breathing for comfort, and patience — it often settles over weeks to a couple of months.\n\nCall 000 for crushing chest pain, pain spreading to the arm or jaw, sweating, nausea, breathlessness, pain on exertion, or a first-ever episode.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
